From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:00:28 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] ws-screen

The WonderSwan Screen section gains a Refresh row: 60 Hz (the default)
sets wswan_60hz_mode, so Beetle Cygne reports 60.38 fps and runs five
frames every four calls on the upstream present path; Native leaves it
off, and the core's own 75.47 fps is paced through ADR 0071's path,
which owes one or two frames a tick on a 59.6 Hz panel. Both play the
game at its own speed. The choice is kept in Config/refresh.txt, becomes
the default, and applies from the next game; a missing line is 60 Hz
and an unknown one is logged and read as 60 Hz. There is no PAL Speed
row: no PAL WonderSwan exists.

A horizontal game is the 224x144 picture at 3x in the middle of the
240x160 canvas (Actual 672x432); a vertical one is 144x224 at 2x in the
middle of 360x240 (Actual 288x448). LCD3x is a 3x shader, so a vertical
game chosen with it draws with none, and says so once in the log.

The 360x240 buffer follows nelynes/slotPlus
(https://github.com/nelynes/slotPlus/commit/ceed887) and the own shader
row its eabb24e (both GPL-3.0).
